{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/733932-linux","id":733932,"title":"Linux?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-27T22:37:16-07:00","id":733932,"title":"Linux?","content":"So, my laptop, which has been dying a slow and annoying death, has finally reached the point where it can barely be used for typing, so I think I'm going to have to get a new one. But, Windows 7 is getting difficult to get, and I loath Windows 8, and refuse to get 10 on philosophical grounds. So, I'm eyeballing Linux.<br /> <br /> A more computer-savvy-than-I friend has mentioned that Linux Mint is probably the distribution I would be best working with, and based on ten minutes of Googling it certainly seems user-friendly enough. Does anyone have any advice for me with regard to Linux? Does it network well with Windows computers (I'm mostly thinking file sharing and printing here)? Any tricks/stumbling blocks I need to avoid or be aware of?<br /> <br /> I <i>kind of</i> know what I'm doing, but when people start talking in terms of packets and bootloaders I start to blink blankly. I know what the terms <i>mean</i> (mostly), just I'm mostly self-taught of the school of 'how can I get this computer to stop exploding' type. And obviously that's almost entirely based on Windows, which may or may not generalise here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:46:51-07:00","id":736043,"title":"","content":"All this depends on your laptop's specs. If you got less than 4gb ram, and a Core 2 Duo or sth in that vain, I suggest you give Lubuntu (or Xubuntu, although I think xfce's development has somewhat slowed down) a go.<br /> <br /> Bootloaders and all that stuff are not really the user's concern. It's mostly useful for dual-booting, and even then, all you need to know is how to google the bootloader's reinstallation. Windows has a bootloader, and Ubuntu has a bootloader as well (GRUB2).<br /> <br /> Also make sure you create a large enough swap partition (twice your RAM size, as a rule of thumb).<br /> <br /> What is your graphics card model?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:48:25-07:00","id":736480,"title":"","content":"Not sure, I'm reasonably sure that part of the reason the laptop has crapped out is due to the hardware becoming insufficient to deal with the demands of programs. It wasn't exactly a powerhouse when I bought it five or six years ago, and when I try to do even the basics it chugs badly. I'm going to double check, but at the most I'm just making this decision earlier than I strictly have to. So I'm getting a new rig which I have yet to decide on the specifics of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T03:36:59-07:00","id":737503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/733932-linux?p=736480#post736480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure, I'm reasonably sure that part of the reason the laptop has crapped out is due to the hardware becoming insufficient to deal with the demands of programs. It wasn't exactly a powerhouse when I bought it five or six years ago, and when I try to do even the basics it chugs badly. I'm going to double check, but at the most I'm just making this decision earlier than I strictly have to. So I'm getting a new rig which I have yet to decide on the specifics of.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Lubuntu is a safer choice (it's Ubuntu, the same base as Linux Mint, with a lighter desktop environment). The installation is pretty straightforward and it uses an app store for most software you might need.<br /> <br /> If you need help with your new machine (parts, brands, and so on), let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:04:58-07:00","id":743367,"title":"","content":"So the laptop I'm eyeballing has a Intel\u00ae Core\u2122 i7 5500U processor (base 2.4GHz, max 3.0GHz), 4GB + 4GB DDR3 RAM, a 1TB hard drive and a NVIDIA GT920M 2GB graphics card (I don't plan to use it for gaming, but I'm not going to turn down a decent video capacity either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) . Total price: $995.<br /> <br /> From the research I've done, it seems like that'd all be more than sufficient to do my word processing and internet browsing for at least a few years.<br /> <br /> It does come with Windows 10, but since I plan to just wipe the drive and drop Linux on it, rather than messing around with the dual-booting thing - maybe later, but for now I'd rather keep things comparatively simple - I don't see that as a major factor? Or is there some kind of issue there I'm missing? I know dual-boots are common, but I always understood that as an 'keeping options open' thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}